SwitchCore patch for azahar-emu/dynarmic a46601580d5512d324104f985b5f0209dc980ddc.

Lets the ARM64 backend use caller-owned code memory with separate executable and
writable views. iOS 26 on TXM devices only executes regions prepared through the
debugger at startup, so the recompiler must take its code cache from a fixed pool
and write it through an alias instead of allocating MAP_JIT memory per instance.
Without the new UserConfig fields the backend behaves as before.

